  StyleBox["candidateID", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "48bd69e0-f146-4541-b272-5840e614efb2"],
 ".",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
  "d096eeb7-f6be-e94c-bc41-f5edb53e1666"]
}], "Usage",
 CellID->869288334,ExpressionUUID->"8c0c78c2-9fb0-ae4a-93cf-63b75807e204"],

Cell["\<\
Tabs: run summary (run ID, seed, state equivalence, rewrite semantics, \
versions, random seed, outcome claims, front sizes, proposal failures, \
performance), candidate table, Pareto front, lineage, strategy weights, front \
history and one candidate (identity, applied operators, status, limits \
reached, front membership, fitness, states graph and fitness trajectory).\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->697067886,ExpressionUUID->"f62d4e9c-371d-3b40-848b-6683b7be1ca4"],

Cell["\<\
By default the candidate tab shows the first solution-front candidate, else \
the first search-front candidate, else the baseline. The option \
\"ParetoMetrics\" -> {metric1, metric2} chooses the plotted metrics; \
Automatic picks two numeric metrics, preferring state count, longest \
derivation and transition count.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->501656965,ExpressionUUID->"3e03b66c-9975-ac48-928d-0ad9fde5a974"],

Cell["\<\
It uses only the data stored in the result; nothing is evolved or evaluated \
again.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->22077013,ExpressionUUID->"ff0d4da6-5489-0e4f-8896-7d4e85440458"]
}, Open  ]],

